    {
      "id": 102,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Downtime fields edited",
      "description": "ONE INCREMENT PER CHANGED FIELD, which is the grain oee.downtime_report_history is written at \u2014 so this and the trail can be reconciled against each other. Flat at zero is the EXPECTED state until the pipeline populates source_event_id (TODOS.md 19): a stop without one cannot be addressed, so the browser disables the action.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (field) (rate(downtime_edits_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{field}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 103,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Downtime edits refused, by cause",
      "description": "approved = a 409 against a signed-off report, which is the freeze working. concurrent = two operators, resolved by the optimistic guard. RESTATED IS THE ONE TO WATCH: the pipeline reloaded the row mid-edit, and the operator's instinct \u2014 retry \u2014 would overwrite a fresh upstream correction. A sustained rate there argues for TODOS.md 38, not a longer retry.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (cause) (rate(downtime_edit_conflicts_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{cause}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 104,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Approval transitions",
      "description": "to=closed is an approve, to=open a reopen. source will read `system` when the 14-day sweeper lands (TODOS.md 31) with no new instrument needed \u2014 which is why this is one counter with labels rather than four counters.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (to, source) (rate(shift_report_transitions_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{to}} / {{source}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 105,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Stale-cache conflicts (409/412)",
      "description": "THE SIGNAL IS NOT 'users double-click'. A conflict means the browser OFFERED an action that was not available \u2014 a stale cache \u2014 and the server answered perfectly correctly and looked entirely healthy while doing it. These counters are the only thing that would ever say so.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(shift_report_transition_conflicts_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "transitions",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(downtime_edit_conflicts_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "downtime edits",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 106,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Has anything ever been edited?",
      "description": "Zero is expected today and is not a fault: source_event_id is unpopulated, so the write path is unreachable rather than unused. Once TODOS.md 19 lands, a persistent zero here means something is wrong with the path rather than with the data.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(downtime_edits_total[$__range])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "field changes in range",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {},
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
