    {
      "id": 111,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Downtime rows dropped from the timeline",
      "description": "A dropped stop did not vanish from the database, it vanished from the CHART \u2014 an open stop against a window that has not started, or a window that resolved wrong. The strip renders without it and says nothing at all. NOTE: inverted rows (end_at before start_at) stopped reaching this counter on 2026-09-02, when the membership predicate began excluding them in Postgres (TODOS.md \u00a710 / \u00a769). A flat zero here is not proof the data is clean \u2014 \u00a770 carries the table-wide check.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(downtime_rows_dropped_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "dropped",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 112,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Time-zone resolution outcomes",
      "description": "A FAILED RESOLUTION STILL RETURNS 200, because TimeZoneResolver serves stale rather than erroring. The consequence is a shift window built from the wrong offset, which moves the 23:00 boundary and misattributes stops between shifts \u2014 the exact class of bug that produced a real shift-3 defect.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 25
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(time_zone_resolutions_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
